 ## Overview
 
-As we launch safer and more capable models, we regularly retire older models. Software relying on OpenAI models may need occasional updates to keep working. Impacted customers will always be notified by email and in our documentation along with blog posts for larger changes.
+As we launch safer and more capable models, we regularly retire older models. Software relying on OpenAI models may need occasional updates to keep working. Impacted customers will always be notified by email and in our documentation.
 
-This page lists all API deprecations, along with recommended replacements.
+Each model has one of three lifecycle states.
 
-To monitor model shutdowns programmatically, call the List models endpoint (`GET /v1/models`) and check each model's optional `shutdown_date` field. When present, this field contains the shutdown date as a `YYYY-MM-DD` string, or `null` if no shutdown date has been announced; the field is also available from the Retrieve a model endpoint.
+- Active. You can use the model through the API. OpenAI hasn't announced its retirement.
+- Deprecated. OpenAI has announced the model's retirement. You can still use it until its shutdown date.
+- Shutdown. The model no longer accepts requests through the standard API.
+
+For deprecation notice periods and help migrating to a replacement model, see the deprecation policy and migration guidance below.
+
+See feature and endpoint deprecations for other upcoming API shutdowns.
+
