+### Historical notes
+
+- Fine-tuned versions of the legacy GPT models shut down in October 2026 followed the same shutdown schedule as their underlying base models.
+- The `codex-mini-latest` shutdown also ended support for the legacy local shell tool. For new integrations, use the shell tool.
+- The Assistants API notice followed the release of the Responses API in March 2025. We first announced plans to retire the Assistants API v1 beta when we released v2 in April 2024.
+- The October 2024 shutdown for fine-tuning training on `babbage-002` and `davinci-002` applied to creating new fine-tuned models. Existing fine-tuned models were unaffected by that change.
+- The June 6, 2024 notice reconfirmed the retirement of `gpt-4-32k-0314`. Starting June 17, 2024, access to the GPT-4-32K and Vision Preview models and the GPT-3.5 Turbo snapshots announced in November 2023 was limited to existing users. Existing fine-tuned models from those GPT-3.5 Turbo snapshots were unaffected by that shutdown.
+- The legacy fine-tunes endpoint shutdown also removed access to models trained with that endpoint. Developers had to train new models through the updated fine-tuning API.
+- The July 2023 announcement covered older GPT-3 and GPT-3.5 models served through the completions endpoint and first-generation text embedding models. See the pricing page for current model pricing.
+- The June 2023 announcement gave an earliest retirement date of June 13, 2024 for the original chat models. Starting January 10, 2024, access was limited to existing users. See the March 2026 shutdown notice for the final shutdown date of `gpt-4-0314`.
